        "original_id": "0dea42e7-c8b6-54f9-85a3-5ceb1b005fec",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: RAF Mount Pleasant, Stanley, East Falkland, Falkland Islands\n- Organizations: Royal Air Force\n- Topics: British military presence, population\n\nFacts:\n- RAF Mount Pleasant is a Royal Air Force station in the British Overseas Territory of the Falkland Islands.\n- RAF Mount Pleasant is also known as Mount Pleasant Airport, Mount Pleasant Complex, or MPA, and it has the codes IATA: MPN and ICAO: EGYP.\n- RAF Mount Pleasant is located on East Falkland about 33 miles southwest of Stanley, the capital of the Falkland Islands.\n- RAF Mount Pleasant is home to between 1,000 and 2,000 British military personnel.\n- On 15 April 2012, the Falkland Islands had a total population of 2,841 on Census Day.\n- At the 2012 census, Stanley had a population of 2,121.",
